-latvian-men-arrested-near-uk-airbase-housing-us-nato-intelligence-operations/articleshow/134795943.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T22:13:38+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134795972,imgsize-212516.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[France student protests escalate in Paris: Clashes erupt, police fire tear gas]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134796050.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/frances-student-stir-intensifies-in-paris-schools-shut-police-fire-tear-gas/articleshow/134796050.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/frances-student-stir-intensifies-in-paris-schools-shut-police-fire-tear-gas/articleshow/134796050.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T22:17:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134796063,imgsize-174678.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Metallica’s job-training programme grows from 10 to 93 US colleges with $17M investment]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134792745.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In 2019, Metallica's All Within My Hands foundation introduced the Metallica Scholars Initiative, aiming to bolster workforce education. Initially partnering with 10 community colleges, the program has significantly grown, reaching 93 learning institutions nationwide. By 2026, this initiative has seen an investment of over $17 million, enhancing technical education and equipping students for rewarding careers. Additionally, it has successfully introduced a similar program in the UK.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2019-metallicas-foundation-launched-a-job-training-initiative-at-10-us-colleges-seven-years-later-its-investment-topped-17-million-and-the-programme-expanded-to-93-colleges-across-all-50-states/articleshow/134792745.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2019-metallicas-foundation-launched-a-job-training-initiative-at-10-us-colleges-seven-years-later-its-investment-topped-17-million-and-the-programme-expanded-to-93-colleges-across-all-50-states/articleshow/134792745.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T22:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134792885,imgsize-116987.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Texas student returns to college after 10 years, earns national leadership honour]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134795640.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-franz-lozano-jr-the-texas-student-who-returned-to-education-after-more-than-a-decade-away-he-is-now-part-of-a-national-award-winning-student-organisation-recognised-for-leadership-service-and-community-engagement/articleshow/134795640.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-franz-lozano-jr-the-texas-student-who-returned-to-education-after-more-than-a-decade-away-he-is-now-part-of-a-national-award-winning-student-organisation-recognised-for-leadership-service-and-community-engagement/articleshow/134795640.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T22:04:08+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134795730,imgsize-785820.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US charges former Venezuela president Maduro with conspiracy to torture opponents]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134794831.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The new allegations accuse Maduro of authorising torture, arbitrary detention and violence against opponents during his time as president. The indictment says thousands of Venezuelans were “harassed, threatened, arrested, prosecuted, assaulted, tortured, or killed” by people acting at the direction of his government. It alleges that methods of abuse included electric shocks, beatings and asphyxiation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-charges-former-venezuela-president-maduro-with-conspiracy-to-torture-opponents/articleshow/134794831.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-charges-former-venezuela-president-maduro-with-conspiracy-to-torture-opponents/articleshow/134794831.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T21:27:04+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134794931,imgsize-68894.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[New lawsuit against Green Card rules: Why separate family members by sending the applicants out of country]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134794056.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/new-lawsuit-against-green-card-rules-why-separate-family-members-by-sending-the-applicants-out-of-country/articleshow/134794056.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/new-lawsuit-against-green-card-rules-why-separate-family-members-by-sending-the-applicants-out-of-country/articleshow/134794056.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T20:36:29+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134794107,imgsize-44994.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Royal Navy sailor charged under UK National Security Act of spying for Russia]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134792797.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/royal-navy-sailor-charged-under-uk-national-security-act-of-spying-for-russia/articleshow/134792797.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/royal-navy-sailor-charged-under-uk-national-security-act-of-spying-for-russia/articleshow/134792797.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T19:38:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134792972,imgsize-35578.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Serena Williams helped build Jamaica school for 80 preschool children in 2016]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134787652.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Serena Williams has taken an admirable step towards education by contributing to the Salt Marsh Basic School in Trelawny, Jamaica. This school provides free preschool education to local children, significantly improving their access to learning. By physically participating in the building process alongside other volunteers, Williams showcased the value of community collaboration in fostering educational growth and ensuring a safe space for the children.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-2016-serena-williams-helped-fund-and-build-a-school-in-jamaica-alongside-charity-partners-and-volunteers-the-salt-marsh-project-was-designed-to-give-80-preschool-children-access-to-free-education/articleshow/134787652.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-2016-serena-williams-helped-fund-and-build-a-school-in-jamaica-alongside-charity-partners-and-volunteers-the-salt-marsh-project-was-designed-to-give-80-preschool-children-access-to-free-education/articleshow/134787652.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T19:57:23+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134787693,imgsize-164952.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California father builds 180-foot backyard roller coaster after son asks for one]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134792695.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A California father constructed a 180-foot roller coaster for his son after the child expressed interest. They spent six weeks working on the project, which cost around $3,500 to complete. The father used the project as an educational opportunity to teach his son about physics and mathematics throughout the construction process. Neighbors became curious and followed the project as it progressed in their backyard.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-california-boy-asked-his-father-for-a-backyard-roller-coaster-and-he-said-yes-six-weeks-and-about-3500-later-a-180-foot-homemade-ride-was-winding-through-the-familys-quarter-acre-yard/articleshow/134792695.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-california-boy-asked-his-father-for-a-backyard-roller-coaster-and-he-said-yes-six-weeks-and-about-3500-later-a-180-foot-homemade-ride-was-winding-through-the-familys-quarter-acre-yard/articleshow/134792695.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T19:35:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134792845,imgsize-2006386.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[How a $5 million fundraising drive and Rockefeller gift helped create Great Smoky Mountains National Park]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134791518.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The establishment of Great Smoky Mountains National Park was a remarkable achievement that required overcoming significant financial challenges due to increasing land prices. Initial fundraising efforts gathered $5 million, but this amount quickly proved insufficient as prices soared. The Rockefeller family stepped in, matching previous contributions with an additional $5 million, allowing for crucial land acquisitions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1928-supporters-had-raised-5-million-for-great-smoky-mountains-national-park-but-rising-land-prices-stalled-the-effort-a-rockefeller-memorial-fund-matched-it-with-another-5-million-helping-make-the-park-possible/articleshow/134791518.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1928-supporters-had-raised-5-million-for-great-smoky-mountains-national-park-but-rising-land-prices-stalled-the-effort-a-rockefeller-memorial-fund-matched-it-with-another-5-million-helping-make-the-park-possible/articleshow/134791518.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T18:40:01+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134791631,imgsize-1214904.cms"/></item></channel></rss>